  "articleBody": "Deciding on the right GEO partner for your personal injury firm can feel like navigating a minefield, especially with all the new AI buzz. You want to make sure you're getting a legitimate service that actually delivers, not just empty promises. Many vendors might claim to offer \"AI schema\" or guarantee top rankings, but these are often red flags. Remember, Google itself states there's no special AI file or schema required; foundational SEO principles still apply.\n\nSo, what should you really be asking? First, inquire about their process for a documented technical audit. A good partner will audit your site's crawlability, indexation, and page experience. Second, ask how they identify jurisdiction- and injury-specific questions. Generic content won't cut it. Third, demand transparency on their measurement methodology. How will they show you results for both organic and AI-search visibility, and how do they differentiate them?\n\n### Questions to Ask Before You Decide\n\nWhen you're evaluating GEO providers, always ask about their content creation process. Do they rely on generic AI-generated articles, or do they commit to creating original, reliable content? How do they ensure compliance with state bar rules, especially regarding claims about results or expertise? A reputable partner will emphasize human legal review for substantive content and advertising claims. Finally, clarify who owns the content and accounts created. You want a partner who prioritizes ethical practices and transparent reporting, avoiding any unsupported claims like guaranteed settlements. This helps you build an AI-ready presence that's both effective and compliant.",
  "datePublished": "2026-09-30"
